\title[Full pinning at degree ten]{Full Pinning at Degree Ten:\\ Exact Type Channels of the Cyclotomic Field $\Q(\zeta_{11})$}
\author{Aristotle}
\date{October 2026}

\begin{document}

\begin{abstract}
For a Galois number field $K/\Q$ and an unramified prime $p$, the \emph{Frobenius type} records how $p$ splits in $K$. We study the information-theoretic channel from a residue observation (such as $p \bmod n$) to the Frobenius type, in the model where Frobenius classes are uniformly distributed (Chebotarev). For the full cyclotomic field $\Q(\zeta_{11})$, of degree ten with cyclic Galois group $C_{10}\cong(\Z/11)^\times$, we prove that the residue $p\bmod 11$ \emph{fully pins} the type:
\[ I(p \bmod 11;\ T) = H(T) = \ltwo 5 - \tfrac35 \approx 1.72193, \]
the type is certain given the residue, and the residue retains exactly $8/5$ bits given the type. These follow from a general \emph{abelian full-pinning law} valid for every finite abelian Galois group, together with the closed form $H(T) = -\sum_{d\mid n}\frac{\varphi(d)}{n}\ltwo\frac{\varphi(d)}{n}$ for every cyclic field. We prove that for every $n$ and every prime $p\nmid n$ the cyclotomic polynomial $\Phi_n$ factors over $\F_p$ into $\varphi(n)/t$ irreducible factors of degree $t=\ord_n(p)$, and that this is the cycle pattern of multiplication by $p$ on $(\Z/n)^\times$. We analyse the tower $\Q\subset\Q(\zeta_{11})^+\subset\Q(\zeta_{11})$: the real quintic subfield is fully pinned with $H(T^+)=\ltwo 5-8/5$, and the tower contributes exactly one bit. For semiprimes $N=pq$ we obtain $I(N\bmod 11;\{T(p),T(q)\}) = \ltwo 5+\frac{12}{25}\ltwo 3-\frac{47}{25}\approx 1.20271$, an exact attenuation of $\frac{32}{25}-\frac{12}{25}\ltwo 3\approx 0.519$ bits relative to a single prime, and we prove that the \emph{which-factor wall} vanishes identically for every finite group whenever the residue is read through the abelianization. All decimal values are certified by exact integer power comparisons.
\end{abstract}

